From 33a67e8362162d34aa26cc851d16636b3965c02c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:34:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 092/274] TileLang V4.1 CSA compression: pooling, rounding and
 RMSNorm in one launch

DeepSeek's compressor arithmetic (ratio 1: norm of each token; ratio 2: the
odd position pools its pair with a per-channel softmax of the gates, rounds to
BF16, then the norm) over the step's rows only. B12X's mla_compress launches a
128-thread block for every token of the batch capacity on every call (8192
blocks and a full latent buffer written per compressor at decode) plus a
pending-ring commit vLLM never reads; vLLM's Triton ring save also spans the
capacity.

- gather_partial_state: vLLM's _load_partial_state, each request's carry.
- compress: one warp a token, 16 values a lane, warp-shuffle sum of squares,
  library exp and rsqrt as the reference computes them (B12X used fast
  approximations); it also saves each live token's ring state, for the rows the
  metadata gives a ring slot (a request's last ring-size rows), a bound the
  kernel keeps itself as well.

Tests compare the latents with DeepSeek's arithmetic (B12X's oracle, within one
BF16 ulp from the reduction order), the carries and short-request ring saves
bit for bit with vLLM's Triton kernels, batch independence and graph replays.

(cherry picked from commit c1e10dce3b43fee9c2272612273df234c39f306b)

